      "confidence": "high",
      "explanation": "The affirmation substitutes presumed unwillingness for evidence about dissenters' motives, discounting their disagreement through a moral defect (E1489–1494). Turek limits this to many cases, and cites people accepting fetal humanity (E1495–1499); that supports a distinction about humanity, but does not establish that they knowingly reject what is right."
